BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-20261127-596@tonight
DTSTAMP:20261125T140232Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261129T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261129T170000
SUMMARY:A Ghost in Your Ear
LOCATION:Audible's Minetta Lane Theatre\, Greenwich Village
DESCRIPTION:When an actor arrives late to a sound studio for a last-minute 
 
audiobook recording session\, he is handed the script of a chilling ghost s
 
tory to read. But as the engineer cues the recording and the evening wears 
 
on\, the horrors slowly begin to escape the page to haunt the studio itself
 
. Fresh from an acclaimed\, sold-out run in London\, A GHOST IN YOUR EAR is
 
 the "truly terrifying headphone horror" (The Guardian) from the darkly bri
 
lliant mind of Tony Award® nominee Jamie Armitage (SIX)\, made in collabor
 
ation with Ben and Max Ringham (ANNA\, National Theatre). A mesmerizing ble
 
nd of gothic horror and psychological thriller\, this cutting-edge theatric
 
al experience uses groundbreaking binaural sound technology to immerse ever
 
y audience member in a haunting world of sound. And at Audible's Minetta La
 
ne Theatre - one of New York's most intimate venues - there's no escaping t
 
he frights. Enter if you dare. Tickets & info: https://www.ticketmaster.com
 
/a-ghost-in-your-ear-new-york-new-york-11-29-2026/event/300064F5E3EAA8DE
URL:https://www.ticketmaster.com/a-ghost-in-your-ear-new-york-new-york-11-2
 
9-2026/event/300064F5E3EAA8DE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-20261127-597@tonight
DTSTAMP:20261125T140232Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261129T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261129T170000
SUMMARY:The Conversation
LOCATION:Astor Place Theatre\, Greenwich Village
DESCRIPTION:THE CONVERSATION follows Marcus (Tony Award-winner Joshua Henry
 
) and Elle (Julia Harriman) from the electric spark of their first date to 
 
move-ins\, milestones\, and the slow accumulation of everything left unsaid
 
. The score\, written by Henry and Harriman\, weaves soul\, R&B\, and moder
 
n pop into bold musical theater storytelling that is intimate\, honest\, an
 
d emotionally gripping. With a book by Nick Green and directed by Tony Awar
 
d-winner Kenny Leon\, The Conversation asks what it takes to choose love\, 
 
even when it hurts\, and what it takes to stay. Tickets & info: https://www
 
.ticketmaster.com/the-conversation-new-york-new-york-11-29-2026/event/03006
 
51FC8031809
URL:https://www.ticketmaster.com/the-conversation-new-york-new-york-11-29-2
 
026/event/0300651FC8031809
END:VEVENT
